nation\": \"Elevations in liver enzymes—particularly SGPT (serum glutamic-pyruvic transaminase)—are consistently used as biomarkers for hepatotoxicity in this community. Both leflunomide and Chuanwu preparations induce measurable increases in these indicators. Leflunomide caused 2–3 fold elevations in liver enzymes in clinical studies, while both raw and processed Chuanwu significantly raised SGPT in rabbit models. SGPT elevation is further codified as an adverse reaction for processed Chuanwu. These findings validate SGPT and related liver enzymes as sensitive and clinically actionable signals for monitoring drug safety, especially in regimens involving these agents [Data: Entities (13802, 13208); Relationships (2327, 1038, 3292, 9398)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community presents a high severity rating due to documented cases of life-threatening adverse reactions (e.g., acute liver necrosis, severe hepatotoxicity) and complex drug-herb interactions affecting vulnerable populations.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782128375, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1559, "prompt_tokens": 7392, "total_tokens": 8951, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Pharmacological and Hepatotoxic Risk Community: Focus on Leflunomide, Chuanwu, and Huaihua\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on several drugs—including leflunomide, processed and raw Chuanwu (Aconiti Radix), and Huaihua (Sophorae Flos)—and their associations with liver toxicity, drug interactions, and contraindications in specific pati